      "title": "Department of Art and Design - Part-time Lecturer(s)",
      "description": "Department of Art and Design - Part-time Lecturer(s) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and about 9,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Art and Design - Part-time Lecturer(s) (Ref: PTL (AAD) 2026-10-09) Responsibilities The appointee(s) will be responsible for teaching AB6101 Valuation of Art and/or AB6004 Sale and Marketing of Art for the Master of Arts in Art Business (MA-AB) programme in the academic year of 2026/27. prepare teaching materials and deliver lectures; mark assignments and provide feedback to students; organis e field trips and other learning activities relevant to the module(s), as appropriate; and work closely with programme director to ensure effective module delivery. Applicants Should possess a doctoral degree in art business, arts management, cultural and creative industries, humanities, social sciences , or any other disciplines related to arts; have a high level of subject knowledge and practical expertise in the relevant academic or professional discipline; have a successful track record of academic or professional experience in tertiary teaching or professional services or relevant industry experience; and have a good command of English and Chinese, with the ability to teach effectively in Putonghua. Applicants without a doctoral degree will be considered if they hold a master’s degree and have a minimum of 3 years of professional experience in a senior role or as a specialist in the relevant fields. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in January 202 7 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 2 5 October 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
