ations for the following position : School of Humanities and Social Science - Part-time Lecturer(s) (Ref: PTCL (SHSS) 2026-10-02) Responsibilities The appointee(s) will be responsible for supervising students for their capstone projects of Master of Arts in Creative Humanities (MA-CH) in the academic year of 2026/27. c onduct individual and group consultations; m ark assignments and creative outputs , and p rovid e feedback to students; and work closely with programme director to ensure effective module delivery Applicants Should possess a doctoral degree in humanities or creative arts-related fields, such as fine art, media art, design and creative writing. be able to teach in Putonghua and provide evidence of Chinese language proficiency (e.g., Medium of Instruction (MOI) of alma mater, Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education Examination (HKDSE) results, Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi (PSC) results or other equivalent qualifications); and possess proven tertiary-level teaching experience and strong student engagement skills. Applicants without a doctoral degree will be considered if they hold a master’s degree and have a minimum of 3 years of professional experience in a senior role or as a specialist in the relevant fields. .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in January 2027 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 18 October 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used 