      "title": "Centre for Innovation and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Centre for Innovation and Entrepreneurship - Project Officer About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and about 9,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Centre for Innovation and Entrepreneurship - Project Officer (Ref: PO (CIE-830008) 2026-10-02) Responsibilities i mplement and coordinate an ongoing funded project related to youth entrepreneurship in the Greater Bay Area (GBA); l iaise with external and internal stakeholders, including alumni and students, for the effective execution of activities related to this project; m anage the project's budget; p repare promotional materials for the project, including website and social media management; and s erve as secretary in committees and work group s. Applicants Should p ossess a bachelor's degree with at least 3 years of work experience, preferably in the higher education sector or in sizable organisations; h ave a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua); have strong computer skills including MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Chinese word-processing ; d emonstrate excellent interpersonal, organisational, and problem-solving skills ; h ave a strong sense of responsibility and commitment and b e capable of multitasking and attentive to details; be able to w ork independently while being an effective team player; and b e willing to work non-office hours and undertake occasional out-of-town trips. Experience with design software such as Canva, and familiarity with the start-up ecosystem in the Greater Bay Area (GBA), e.g. incubators, accelerators, and entrepreneurship support organisations will be an advantage. Applicants with less work experience will be considered as Assistant Project Officer. .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicants should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 18 October 202 6 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer Apply Now!"
