      "title": "Department of Computer Science - Part-time Lecturer(s)",
      "description": "Department of Computer Science - Part-time Lecturer(s) About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and about 9,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Computer Science - Part-time Lecturer(s) (Ref: PTL (COM) 2026-10-16) Responsibilities The appointee(s) will be responsible for teaching one or more of the following undergraduate modules: COM3110 Backend Web Development Subject areas include data serialization and management, building the backend, and modern backend development practices. COM3112 Game Development Subject areas include game mechanics, using game engine, design patterns in game development, and artificial intelligence in games. Applicants Should Applicants should have a master’s degree or above in related disciplines. Relevant teaching experience at university level is preferred. Applicants with a bachelor’s degree and tertiary teaching experience or industrial experience in relevant fields will also be considered. .................................................................................................................................................................. Please indicate clearly which of the above modules you can teach . The appointee is expected to assume duty in January 2027 . Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ to apply for the position. Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
