      "title": "Department of Mathematics, Statistics and Insurance – Assistant Manager",
      "description": "Department of Mathematics, Statistics and Insurance – Assistant Manager About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and about 9,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Department of Mathematics, Statistics and Insurance – Assistant Manager (Ref: AM (MSI) 2026-10-23) Responsibilities provide administrative support to the Department, including but not limited to programme operation, teaching deployment, class timetabling, module registration and quality assurance matters (e.g. re-accreditation exercise); oversee the Department’s annual budget and expenditure; coordinate Department-related activities, such as research seminar and international conference; prepare proposals, policies, papers and reports on Department-related matters; liaise closely with internal and external stakeholders to support the administration of the Department and foster collaboration on various initiatives; provide secretariat support to Department committees and working groups; and supervise junior administrative staff of the Department. Applicants Should possess a bachelor’s degree with at least 6 years of relevant work experience, preferably in administering academic programmes within the tertiary education sector; be proficient in computer applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Chinese word processing; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Cantonese and Putonghua ; possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills; and be a fast learner, self-motivated, a good team player, and capable of working independently with a strong sense of responsibility . .................................................................................................................................................................. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 8 November 2026. Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    },
    "https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/opening/content.php?id=3908": {
      "title": "Project Assistant (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Project Assistant (Part-Time) – School of Transdisciplinary Studies About the University The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong (HSUHK) is a non-profit private liberal-arts-oriented university with six Schools (Business, Communication, Decision Sciences, Humanities and Social Science, Translation and Foreign Languages, and Transdisciplinary Studies), and about 9,000 full-time undergraduate and postgraduate students. With its unique “Liberal + Professional” education model, HSUHK nurtures caring professionals with a global vision and responsible leadership. Aspiring to be a leading private university in the region, HSUHK prioritises stellar undergraduate education and research informed postgraduate education, supported by excellent student learning experience, impactful research and purposeful engagement. HSUHK places strategic importance on regional engagement and international partnership, which create a productive learning and research environment for students and scholars working creatively and innovatively with a strong interdisciplinary orientation. HSUHK has earned various international recognitions. In the AppliedHE’s ALL ASIA Private University Ranking 2026, it secured 7th place across Chinese Mainland, Hong Kong and Macau. HSUHK ranked 23rd in both Business and Management and Economics and Finance and 24th in Social Sciences and Humanities among this region’s top universities in the Research.com Top Universities and Top Scientists Rankings 2026. The MSc in Global Supply Chain Management programme achieved 84th place globally in the QS International Trade Rankings 2025. Additionally, HSUHK’s School of Business obtained AACSB International accreditation in 2023, a mark of excellence held by only 6% of the world’s leading business schools. HSUHK was also ranked among the top 200 worldwide on “Quality Education” and “Decent Work and Economic Growth” in the Times Higher Education University Impact Rankings 2021. The University now invites applications for the following position : Project Assistant (Part-Time) – School of Transdisciplinary Studies (Ref: PA (STS) 2026-10-23) Responsibilities a ssist in planning, orga nis ing, and coordinating workshops, seminars, and other project-related activities ; l iaise with speakers, participants and related parties to ensure all logistical arrangements are in place ; p repare and manage event materials, invitations, and communications ; and m aintain project schedules and timelines to ensure timely completion of tasks . Applicants Should possess a recognised bachelor’s degree ; preferably have relevant experience in project management, event management, communications, or related fields; demonstrate g ood communication and interpersonal skills ; be able to work independently and collaboratively within a team; and be p roficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and comfortable using online collaboration tools . .................................................................................................................................................................. The appointee is expected to assume duty in December 2026. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interested applicant should visit this link https://recruit.hsu.edu.hk/ and apply on or before 8 November 2026 . Review of applications will begin soon until the position is filled. The University reserves the right not to fill the position in this exercise. Applicants who are not invited to an interview within three months may consider their applications unsuccessful.  All information received will be treated in strict confidence, and the data collected will be used for recruitment purpose s only .  The Personal Information Collection Statement will be provided upon request. The Hang Seng University of Hong Kong, incorporated in Hong Kong with limited liability by guarantee, is an equal opportunity employer. Apply Now!"
    }
